[{:db/id -1, :readme/name "ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico", :readme/source "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka/data/ghosthacker-shiropico", :readme/note "Split from ai-gftd-mangaka for west-managed project ownership. SHIRO & PICO is a sibling work to Ren's Ghost Hacker (`orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker`, `orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka/data/ghosthacker`) in the same GFTD cyber universe (\"information is physical\" / Landauer's principle), aimed at global kids' audiences (India / Gulf-MENA). See SERIES-BIBLE.md. Binary assets (character refs, generated panels, motion comic) live in a separate DataLad dataset `~/gftdcojp/ghosthacker-shiropico-assets` (see ASSETS-DATALAD.md), not in this repo.", :readme/engine-note "Content is engine-agnostic and consumed by two candidate pipelines: `pipeline-specs.json` was authored against ai-gftd-mangaka's storyboardFromPrompt (2D panel) convention, but SHIRO & PICO is structurally an anime, not a manga (11-min episodes, VOICEVOX voice acting, OP/ED, motion comic) — `orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka`'s work/episode/scene/**cut** domain model (`clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc`, 12-stage production pipeline: script->storyboard->layout->keyAnim->inbetween->colorDesign->finish->background->composite->edit->sound->delivery) is the better structural fit, and animeka's own test fixture (`clj/test/animeka/core_test.cljc`) already uses \"Shiro Pico\" / `work-shiro` as its canonical example work. Treat animeka as the primary intended production engine; mangaka's storyboardFromPrompt is a secondary/legacy path pending reconciliation. See ADR-2607011816."}]